t(22, 1345, """Our Lord, You have given us of everything by making us know Your Oneness, so You delighted our hearts that You are One, Unique, Single, Self-Sufficient, with no partner, no rival, no likeness, no child and no consort. We were happy, O our Lord, and rejoiced with the greatest joy when we knew and recognized that we worship You alone, submit to You alone, and rub our noses and foreheads in the dust for You alone. You honored us and raised our worth when our faces prostrated to You with the prostration of the worshippers who rub their noses in the dust; You ennobled us by our lowliness before You, and raised us by our poverty to You. And You favored us by making us know how to rub our noses in the dust for You, prostrating and submissive, lowly before Your Lordship and Your Divinity, sanctifying Your Exalted Self, and surrendering to Your decrees that govern us with the Lord's rule over the servant. You made us understand by Your gentleness, and made us know by the beauty of Your love, that all You wrote for us before You created us was good for us, and that all we meet of Your decrees governing us is for our benefit; whoever gives thanks is rewarded, and whoever resents loses. O Allah, make the hearts of Your servants firm upon Your will, be gentle with their weakness when they do not know Your rulings, and make their worldly life a bridge of well-being until they reach Your abode of permanence.

O Allah, amen, O Lord, and for our offspring, our loved ones, our families, and the Muslim men and Muslim women""")

