t(24, 95, """O noble ones: if a servant whom Allah chose and raised had been harmed in himself, weakened and humiliated, and then Allah empowered him, would you see him forgiving and pardoning, or retaliating and vengeful? Such are the souls of the chosen: they withdraw to the will of their Great Lord, not to their own judgments, in their disputes and in the wrongs done to them, because on earth they carry a spark of the light of prophethood, and draw inspiration from the path of the prophets, their maturity, their wisdom and the breadth of their chests.

And I find in some of the replies here on the channel, increasing day after day, a number of brothers and sisters in pain from an injustice that befell them, which makes their hearts ache all the time, with distress wrapping their lives. If the chosenness of guidance has been realized in them, and they have been enabled to know the Great Lord, holy are His names and attributes, exalted in the heavens and the earth, and highly exalted, then let them draw inspiration from this post, which I publish out of love for them and a desire to supply them with beneficial good that will make them stronger on earth when they belittle what has passed and magnify what is to come, magnifying it with the welcome of the empowered knower (man/woman) whom Allah the Exalted shaped with the shaping of the knowers, not the shaping of the memorizers. For the reformers on earth are captives of the will of Allah the Exalted, not of the will of their own souls, when they wish to help and elevate the soul. For reform on earth is absolutely the greatest work a person does, because it is worship, and there is nothing greater than worship. Reform on earth is a ruby, and turning away from the foolish and the stupid makes the ruby shine more and more.""")

