t(27, 985, """If people gathered around a well whose water had overflowed, and every time they took from it, its water kept overflowing; such is the overflowing of wealth in the future of the Ummah!

From Abu Hurayra, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: the Prophet ﷺ said: «The Hour will not come until wealth increases among you and overflows, until the owner of wealth is worried about who will accept his charity...». Its chain: agreed upon (narrated by al-Bukhari and Muslim).

Overflows (yafid): the word is taken from "the overflowing of water", and what is meant here is that wealth increases so greatly that it exceeds people's consumption needs, exactly like water that fills the vessel, then pours and runs over its sides because of its abundance.

Scatters wealth by handfuls: that is, he gives wealth by scooping it generously with his hand because of its great abundance, and pours it out to people without bothering to count or reckon it.""")

