t(28, 140, """The sons of Isaac are two branches: the Jews, sons of Jacob, peace be upon him; and the second branch is the Romans, sons of Esau. As for the saying that not a single man of the Children of Israel remains on earth today, this is an inferential absurdity that it is not possible at all to waste time discussing, and we have no need to waste our time on it. As for the 70 thousand conquerors being a mixture of the sons of Jacob, peace be upon him, Jews of correct lineage, and the sons of Esau among the Romans, both groups having entered Islam before the Great Battle and before the future conquest of Constantinople, this too is an acceptable and not objectionable view. However, I favor by ijtihad that the 70 thousand are of the sons of Jacob, peace be upon him, who become Muslim at the end of time - and Allah the Exalted is Most High and Most Knowing - or of their children who grow up raised on Islam and will be 17, 20 or 22 years old at the conquest of Constantinople.

As for the 70 thousand being a human composite of Muslim Romans and Jews, this too is possible, because the Prophet ﷺ and his family used the word Romans and the word Jews in other hadiths, but in this noble hadith he did not specify, and used a word that may comprise Muslim Romans and Jews together; and the element of Muslim Jews in the 70 thousand may outweigh numerically the element of Muslim Romans.""")

