t(30, 2440, """In light of the current frivolity, the Ummah today needs a program to correct the behavior of nominal conversion to Islam for the purpose of marrying a Muslim woman, and it is a program whose application is obligatory by Shariah, not optional.""")

t(31, 60, """The suitor who has just become Muslim should be required to observe a period of no less than 3 to 6 months between the date of pronouncing the two testimonies and the date of the marriage contract.
The aim of this is to break the idea of "speed" and end the formula "become Muslim today and marry a Muslim woman 5 minutes later", which pushes the unserious person to withdraw at once if the matter was merely a trick to reach a Muslim woman.

The new Muslim who wishes to marry a Muslim woman should be required to join an educational and practical program supervised by the Ministry of Endowments or the Dar al-Ifta, which includes:

Mandatory in-person attendance: set hours weekly to study creed, purification, prayer and the rules of the family in Islam.

The "religious mentor" system: the new convert is assigned a mentor (the imam of the neighborhood mosque) who accompanies him during these months and testifies to his conduct (such as his commitment to attending Friday and congregational prayers, and the change in his lifestyle).

Before the marriage registrar is allowed to write the contract, the suitor must pass an official assessment:

Knowledge test: a simple assessment proving his practical understanding of the acts of worship and the rights of the Muslim wife.

Personal interview: a committee of judges and psychological and Shariah counselors studies the suitor's case to make sure of his seriousness.

Issuing a "marriage eligibility certificate for converts": without this government certificate, the marriage contract is considered administratively void and is not registered in the courts.

How does this program solve the problem?

It filters out the unserious: the man who wants to use Islam as a "pass" only to reach a Muslim woman - and the cases are in the millions in our time - will not bear committing to a program extending over several months with tests and behavioral follow-up.

It protects the girl and her family: it gives the family a neutral official body that assesses with them the appearance of the man's religion and character before getting entangled in the marriage.

It preserves the dignity of the religion: it prevents turning the rite of declaring Islam into a formal procedure taking a few minutes for the purpose of reaching a Muslim woman.""")

h(31, 1800, """Nominal Islam for the purpose of marriage is a violation of sanctities!""")

